<title>BELGIUM: CYCLING-LEADING PLACINGS IN THE PARIS-BRUSSELS RACE.</title>
<headline>CYCLING-LEADING PLACINGS IN THE PARIS-BRUSSELS RACE.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-09-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading placings in the 247-km</p>
<p>Paris-Brussels cycle race on Saturday:</p>
<p>1. Andrea Tafi (Italy) Mapei-GB  6 hours 15 minutes 0 seconds</p>
<p> 2. Johan Museeuw (Belgium) Mapei-GB	1:51 behind</p>
<p>3. Michele Bartoli (Italy) MG-Technogym  </p>
<p> 4. Andrei Tchmile (Ukraine) Lotto	  both same time</p>
<p> 5. Johan Capiot (Belgium) Collstrop	2:09</p>
<p> 6. Wilfried Peeters (Belgium) Mapei-GB   2:18</p>
<p>7. Lars Michaelsen (Denmark) Festina-Lotus</p>
<p>8. Franco Ballerini (Italy) Mapei-GB</p>
<p> 9. Rolf Sorensen (Denmark) Rabobank    all same time as Peeters</p>
<p> 10. Nico Eeckhout (Belgium) Collstrop    8:01.</p>
</text>
